.TH "OPENCLIGEN" "1" "" "opencligen devel" "opencligen"
.SH NAME
opencligen \- Validate OpenCLI descriptions and generate code and docs from them
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B opencligen
[options] <command>
.SH DESCRIPTION
opencligen validates OpenCLI descriptions (https://opencli.org/) against the OpenCLI schema and its own rules, and generates a urfave/cli v3 command tree in Go, a Markdown reference or a man page from them.
.PP
The x- metadata it understands is described in docs/extensions.md.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-lenient\fR
Report problems that can be worked around as warnings instead of errors: x- metadata that cannot be typed, and features the output cannot express.
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-c\-limits\fR
Accept C limit constants such as INT_MAX, -FLT_MAX or I64_MIN in x-range and x-default.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS "opencligen validate"
.B opencligen validate
[options] <spec>
.PP
Check a description against the OpenCLI schema and opencligen's rules
.PP
\fBArguments:\fR
.TP
\fIspec\fR
Required. The OpenCLI description, a JSON file
.PP
\fBExamples:\fR
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
opencligen validate cli.json
opencligen validate --lenient --allow-c-limits ffmpeg.json
.fi
.RE
.SS "opencligen urfave"
.B opencligen urfave
[options] <spec>
.PP
Generate a github.com/urfave/cli/v3 command tree in Go
.PP
The generated file declares a Handlers interface with one method per runnable command and a New function that builds the command tree wired to it.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-output\fR, \fB\-o\fR \fI<file>\fR
Output file, or - for standard output (default: -)
.TP
\fB\-\-package\fR \fI<name>\fR
Package name of the generated file (default: cli)
.TP
\fB\-\-source\fR \fI<name>\fR
Document name mentioned in the generated header; defaults to the spec path
.PP
\fBArguments:\fR
.TP
\fIspec\fR
Required. The OpenCLI description, a JSON file
.PP
\fBExamples:\fR
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
opencligen urfave -o internal/cli/cli.gen.go --package cli cli.json
.fi
.RE
.SS "opencligen markdown"
.B opencligen markdown
[options] <spec>
.PP
Generate a Markdown reference
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-output\fR, \fB\-o\fR \fI<file>\fR
Output file, or - for standard output (default: -)
.TP
\fB\-\-hidden\fR
Document hidden commands, options and arguments
.PP
\fBArguments:\fR
.TP
\fIspec\fR
Required. The OpenCLI description, a JSON file
.PP
\fBExamples:\fR
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
opencligen markdown -o docs/cli.md cli.json
.fi
.RE
.SS "opencligen man"
.B opencligen man
[options] <spec>
.PP
Generate a roff man page
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-output\fR, \fB\-o\fR \fI<file>\fR
Output file, or - for standard output (default: -)
.TP
\fB\-\-section\fR \fI<n>\fR
Manual section (default: 1)
.TP
\fB\-\-date\fR \fI<date>\fR
Date shown in the page footer; empty by default for reproducible output
.TP
\fB\-\-hidden\fR
Document hidden commands, options and arguments
.PP
\fBArguments:\fR
.TP
\fIspec\fR
Required. The OpenCLI description, a JSON file
.PP
\fBExamples:\fR
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
opencligen man -o docs/mytool.1 cli.json
man -l docs/mytool.1
.fi
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
\fB0\fR
Success
.TP
\fB1\fR
The description has errors, or the output cannot be generated
.TP
\fB2\fR
Invalid usage
.SH SEE ALSO
Contact: https://github.com/angrifel/opencligen
